import tests/games/three_dimensional.dl

the city block size means: 48.0
the city road width means: 12.0
the city lot size means: (the city block size - the city road width) / 2.0

to get the center of city lot {floating-point number:column} {floating-point number:row}:
    set {block column} to the floor of (column / 2.0)
    set {block row} to the floor of (row / 2.0)
    set {local column} to column - (block column * 2.0)
    set {local row} to row - (block row * 2.0)
    return a position with x (((block column * the city block size) + the city road width) + ((local column + 0.5) * the city lot size)), y 0.0 and z (((block row * the city block size) + the city road width) + ((local row + 0.5) * the city lot size))
